1
00:00:14,541 --> 00:00:16,541
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:43,041 --> 00:00:44,874
MIRACLES OF THE ER

3
00:00:44,875 --> 00:00:47,375
A DOCTOR'S CHOICE

4
00:00:49,458 --> 00:00:50,707
CHENG-CHUN

5
00:00:50,708 --> 00:00:52,041
[Yu-hua sobbing]

6
00:00:56,958 --> 00:00:59,207
- [gasps]
- [brakes screech]

7
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:00,707
- [man gasps]
- [girl screams]

8
00:01:00,708 --> 00:01:01,707
[man groans]

9
00:01:01,708 --> 00:01:03,874
[girl] Dad! Are you okay?

10
00:01:03,875 --> 00:01:05,958
- [man coughs]
- [girl] Dad!

11
00:01:07,208 --> 00:01:08,749
Hey. Are you okay?

12
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:10,249
I'm fine. My dad's hurt.

13
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:11,791
Sir, can you hear me?

14
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:14,165
I'm fine. [coughs]

15
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:16,040
- You're fine?
- [man] Yeah.

16
00:01:16,041 --> 00:01:18,040
[coughs]

17
00:01:18,041 --> 00:01:19,749
[girl] Dad, are you okay?

18
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:21,541
[man coughs]

19
00:01:22,208 --> 00:01:23,875
[alarm blaring]

20
00:01:30,291 --> 00:01:31,666
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

21
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:35,249
[Hsiu-ju] What are you doing here?

22
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:36,624
Is the hearing done?

23
00:01:36,625 --> 00:01:39,290
I'll tell you later.
Shortness of breath, likely pneumonia.

24
00:01:39,291 --> 00:01:41,540
O2 mask, take a CBC, biochem,

25
00:01:41,541 --> 00:01:43,332
- gas, blood culture, and X-ray.
- Okay.

26
00:01:43,333 --> 00:01:45,457
Tang Hsi, Tang Hsi,
this is the patient's daughter.

27
00:01:45,458 --> 00:01:46,665
- Take care of her.
- Yeah.

28
00:01:46,666 --> 00:01:47,749
WU MING-CHIN

29
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:49,666
[Yu-hua] Well, that explains the cough.

30
00:01:50,875 --> 00:01:52,416
Lung to lung mets.

31
00:01:53,458 --> 00:01:55,415
It's a return of his lung cancer.

32
00:01:55,416 --> 00:01:57,124
Keep a close eye on him, okay?

33
00:01:57,125 --> 00:01:59,750
- Let me know if anything changes.
- [Hsi] Okay.

34
00:02:10,333 --> 00:02:11,166
Hey.

35
00:02:11,916 --> 00:02:13,332
You didn't tell me before.

36
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:14,290
How'd the hearing go?

37
00:02:14,291 --> 00:02:16,916
Like being on shift
with Dr. Cheng times ten.

38
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:18,708
What?

39
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:20,333
That bad?

40
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,291
You have no idea.

41
00:02:24,916 --> 00:02:25,791
You're not alone.

42
00:02:26,375 --> 00:02:27,916
[lighthearted music playing]

43
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:34,457
[Hsiu-ju] Why don't you go home and rest?

44
00:02:34,458 --> 00:02:35,749
No, I'm okay.

45
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:38,165
I'm waiting on the report
for the lung cancer patient.

46
00:02:38,166 --> 00:02:40,499
[Tung-yen] I just wanna confirm
that the drainage is complete.

47
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,583
- This might be a bit sensitive.
- [groans softly]

48
00:02:45,541 --> 00:02:46,833
Okay, it all looks clear.

49
00:02:47,416 --> 00:02:48,375
Mmm-hmm.

50
00:02:49,083 --> 00:02:50,541
Well, that's a relief.

51
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:53,124
- It feels so much better.
- [old woman] Oh, yes.

52
00:02:53,125 --> 00:02:54,415
Thank you, Dr. Chiang.

53
00:02:54,416 --> 00:02:55,665
Mmm-hmm.

54
00:02:55,666 --> 00:02:57,915
[old woman] Don't you just wish
he was our family doctor?

55
00:02:57,916 --> 00:03:00,332
- Hey. Could you, uh...
- Oh, yes.

56
00:03:00,333 --> 00:03:03,165
- Uh, doctor. Please wait.
- Hmm?

57
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:04,958
We thought you might like these.

58
00:03:05,583 --> 00:03:06,707
Oh, that's okay, really.

59
00:03:06,708 --> 00:03:08,082
You gotta try.

60
00:03:08,083 --> 00:03:10,707
This ox-tongue pastry,
you'll never taste anything better.

61
00:03:10,708 --> 00:03:12,082
Don't be shy.

62
00:03:12,083 --> 00:03:14,833
My husband insists
that you're the best doctor here.

63
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:17,957
As long as it's you he sees,
he'll be at peace.

64
00:03:17,958 --> 00:03:19,332
[old man chuckles]

65
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:20,666
Thank you so much.

66
00:03:21,541 --> 00:03:22,375
Thank you.

67
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:28,124
- [man grunts]
- [woman screams]

68
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:29,415
Got an injury out here.

69
00:03:29,416 --> 00:03:31,000
Get some help. Come on!

70
00:03:32,291 --> 00:03:33,874
- [Hsiu-ju] Excuse us.
- Out of the way.

71
00:03:33,875 --> 00:03:34,915
Trauma Blue!

72
00:03:34,916 --> 00:03:37,457
[intense music playing]

73
00:03:37,458 --> 00:03:38,916
Place two IV lines first.

74
00:03:39,416 --> 00:03:41,165
Let's get four units of whole blood.

75
00:03:41,166 --> 00:03:43,082
- Tung-yen, place the CVC.
- Okay.

76
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:44,915
- Chao-i, prep for intubation. Let's go.
- Yep.

77
00:03:44,916 --> 00:03:46,166
Excuse me.

78
00:03:50,583 --> 00:03:51,458
Blood's here.

79
00:03:58,375 --> 00:03:59,790
[Cheng-chun] He's lost too much blood.

80
00:03:59,791 --> 00:04:01,540
His heart's gonna stop any moment.

81
00:04:01,541 --> 00:04:03,457
- Let's get more gauze here.
- [Hsiu-ju] Okay.

82
00:04:03,458 --> 00:04:05,041
- CVC come on.
- On it.

83
00:04:06,458 --> 00:04:11,208
CVC
CENTRAL LINE OF TRANSFUSION

84
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:13,208
[machine beeping]

85
00:04:31,125 --> 00:04:32,375
[Tung-yen] I can't get it in.

86
00:04:33,375 --> 00:04:35,291
[Cheng-chun] Okay. Try it again.

87
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:37,833
[exhales]

88
00:04:42,458 --> 00:04:43,291
[Chao-i] More gauze.

89
00:04:46,208 --> 00:04:47,666
[Hsiu-ju] Heart rate keeps dropping.

90
00:04:50,041 --> 00:04:51,749
[machine beeping rapidly]

91
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,208
[Chao-i] Bradycardia.

92
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:56,583
Asystole.

93
00:04:57,625 --> 00:04:59,999
CPR. Epi, one milligram, IV stat.

94
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Got it.

95
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:03,582
Leave it now. I'll try.

96
00:05:03,583 --> 00:05:05,499
- Give it to me.
- [Cheng-chun] No, let him do it.

97
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:06,624
He needs to learn.

98
00:05:06,625 --> 00:05:07,625
Again.

99
00:05:13,416 --> 00:05:15,957
[Hsiang-chun] Epi, one milligram, IV push.

100
00:05:15,958 --> 00:05:17,041
[Chao-i] Okay.

101
00:05:19,583 --> 00:05:21,249
- [Tung-yen] Hold compressions.
- Okay.

102
00:05:21,250 --> 00:05:24,750
[machine beeping rapidly]

103
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,291
We're good.

104
00:05:35,083 --> 00:05:36,416
Run blood wide open.

105
00:05:46,708 --> 00:05:47,707
All done.

106
00:05:47,708 --> 00:05:48,707
Hold compressions.

107
00:05:48,708 --> 00:05:49,708
[Chao-i] Okay.

108
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:51,832
Still no pulse.

109
00:05:51,833 --> 00:05:53,125
[Tung-yen] Here, I'll take over.

110
00:05:53,708 --> 00:05:54,916
[Yuan-ting] Three, two, one.

111
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:57,791
[pants]

112
00:06:04,791 --> 00:06:05,749
Two minutes.

113
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:07,583
[machine beeping rapidly]

114
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:10,915
We got a pulse.

115
00:06:10,916 --> 00:06:13,125
- [Cheng-chun] Take his BP.
- [Yuan-ting] On it.

116
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:18,082
[Cheng-chun] The wound here
didn't penetrate the body cavity.

117
00:06:18,083 --> 00:06:19,290
Same here.

118
00:06:19,291 --> 00:06:21,124
BP 100 over 70.

119
00:06:21,125 --> 00:06:22,416
Vital signs are back.

120
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,791
Let's get a CT scan. Book the ICU.

121
00:06:25,291 --> 00:06:26,582
Chao-i, deal with the wounds.

122
00:06:26,583 --> 00:06:27,541
[Chao-i] Okay.

123
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:39,708
[gasps]

124
00:06:49,333 --> 00:06:50,208
[Tung-yen] Sir.

125
00:06:50,916 --> 00:06:53,082
Are you visiting someone? Can I help you?

126
00:06:53,083 --> 00:06:55,916
Did a person with multiple knife wounds
come through here?

127
00:07:06,708 --> 00:07:07,791
This way, please.

128
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:11,082
Godmother,
the Nansha Association did this.

129
00:07:11,083 --> 00:07:12,540
[sighs wearily]

130
00:07:12,541 --> 00:07:14,999
- How did all this happen?
- I'm fine.

131
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,208
I was lucky.

132
00:07:20,416 --> 00:07:21,374
Doctor.

133
00:07:21,375 --> 00:07:22,458
Excuse me.

134
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,499
What's my husband's situation?

135
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:26,749
The bleeding from his external wounds
has been treated.

136
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:28,832
His condition's more or less stabilized.

137
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:31,291
And once a bed opens up,
he'll go to the ICU.

138
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:34,708
Did ICH show up in the scan?

139
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:36,958
No. Are you a doctor?

140
00:07:42,708 --> 00:07:43,541
Kuei-sheng.

141
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:46,582
We've weathered all kinds of storms.

142
00:07:46,583 --> 00:07:48,291
You'll be fine.

143
00:07:49,166 --> 00:07:51,416
I'll take revenge
for what's happened here.

144
00:07:52,416 --> 00:07:56,083
[ominous music playing]

145
00:08:05,916 --> 00:08:08,541
UNBROKEN

146
00:08:18,375 --> 00:08:20,040
[Hsiang-chun]
What's wrong with Dr. Chiang?

147
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:21,208
[Geng-ming] Hmm. I don't know.

148
00:08:24,958 --> 00:08:26,708
[young Tung-yen] <i>Dad, I'm home.</i>

149
00:08:30,208 --> 00:08:32,375
Dad, what are you doing? Come down!

150
00:08:33,375 --> 00:08:34,457
Come down now.

151
00:08:34,458 --> 00:08:35,665
Dad!

152
00:08:35,666 --> 00:08:36,625
Come down!

153
00:08:37,458 --> 00:08:38,915
- See what happens
- Help me!

154
00:08:38,916 --> 00:08:40,249
when you don't pay us back.

155
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:42,665
[young Tung-yen]
Please, help me save my dad.

156
00:08:42,666 --> 00:08:43,707
Help me now!

157
00:08:43,708 --> 00:08:45,207
- Oh, and your house,
- Please!

158
00:08:45,208 --> 00:08:46,790
- he already mortgaged it to me.
- Help me!

159
00:08:46,791 --> 00:08:49,125
- So it's mine now.
- Why aren't you helping me?

160
00:08:49,958 --> 00:08:52,708
[straining, crying] Save my dad!

161
00:08:53,416 --> 00:08:54,916
Someone save my dad!

162
00:08:55,666 --> 00:08:57,500
<i>Someone</i>, <i>please help me!</i>

163
00:08:58,208 --> 00:08:59,416
<i>Dad!</i>

164
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:03,708
Mr. Wu.

165
00:09:04,458 --> 00:09:05,707
How are you feeling?

166
00:09:05,708 --> 00:09:07,415
Are you the attending doctor?

167
00:09:07,416 --> 00:09:08,665
- Yeah.
- I wanna be discharged.

168
00:09:08,666 --> 00:09:10,415
Wait, you can't be discharged.

169
00:09:10,416 --> 00:09:12,290
Your lung cancer's back.

170
00:09:12,291 --> 00:09:14,207
We've already asked oncology
to come see you.

171
00:09:14,208 --> 00:09:16,249
I said I wanna go. Do you understand me?

172
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:18,166
[girl] Dad, come on. You've been hurt.

173
00:09:18,833 --> 00:09:19,999
Let her help, okay?

174
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,665
Oh, but sweetheart, if I don't leave now,

175
00:09:21,666 --> 00:09:24,000
- I won't get the stall open in time.
- Mr. Wu, please.

176
00:09:24,625 --> 00:09:26,165
You're not in a good way right now.

177
00:09:26,166 --> 00:09:27,790
Now, if we let you go,

178
00:09:27,791 --> 00:09:29,707
your daughter will have to bring you back.

179
00:09:29,708 --> 00:09:31,457
This is my suggestion.

180
00:09:31,458 --> 00:09:34,166
Don't worry about getting to work.
For now, okay?

181
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:37,458
You're really sure? That I'll get better?

182
00:09:38,583 --> 00:09:40,083
- [somber music playing]
- [coughing]

183
00:09:41,041 --> 00:09:43,957
If I don't go to work today,
I won't have the money to be here.

184
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,958
Hospitals are expensive places.

185
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:48,457
Do you have a waiver? I'll just sign that.

186
00:09:48,458 --> 00:09:49,499
- Come on.
- Mr. Wu, please.

187
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,999
Mr. Wu. You can't get a place
in the insurance ward now,

188
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
but we can start treatment
in the observation area.

189
00:09:55,666 --> 00:09:57,915
If your condition improves,
you can get discharged.

190
00:09:57,916 --> 00:10:00,665
And you won't be charged
for hospitalization.

191
00:10:00,666 --> 00:10:01,958
[girl] Dad, please.

192
00:10:03,041 --> 00:10:05,499
Listen to the doctor. Come on.

193
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:08,291
[labored breathing]

194
00:10:12,625 --> 00:10:13,583
All right.

195
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:15,958
Okay.

196
00:10:21,583 --> 00:10:24,083
- So, you got the cancer patient to stay.
- Mmm.

197
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:27,624
It's so good you managed to do that.

198
00:10:27,625 --> 00:10:29,083
Would have been dangerous to leave.

199
00:10:30,583 --> 00:10:32,708
- If you go near there later...
- Yeah, I'll take care of him.

200
00:10:33,541 --> 00:10:35,000
I'll swing by now.

201
00:10:36,083 --> 00:10:36,916
Hey!

202
00:10:37,541 --> 00:10:38,874
Thank you.

203
00:10:38,875 --> 00:10:40,375
[chuckles softly]

204
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:49,416
Hsiang-chun.

205
00:10:52,083 --> 00:10:54,665
During change of route today,
was the medicine quantity right?

206
00:10:54,666 --> 00:10:56,750
Yeah, I checked it myself.

207
00:10:57,375 --> 00:10:58,291
What's wrong?

208
00:10:59,208 --> 00:11:01,875
[Su-ching] Uh, I noticed
that some items were missing.

209
00:11:03,708 --> 00:11:05,957
Two bottles of KCL.

210
00:11:05,958 --> 00:11:07,791
Could they have been misplaced though?

211
00:11:08,416 --> 00:11:09,665
Well, I guess they might have.

212
00:11:09,666 --> 00:11:11,624
But if they're not used correctly,

213
00:11:11,625 --> 00:11:13,790
KCL can cause asystole.

214
00:11:13,791 --> 00:11:15,790
A patient could just die suddenly.

215
00:11:15,791 --> 00:11:17,207
[gasps]

216
00:11:17,208 --> 00:11:18,500
I'll search again.

217
00:11:23,708 --> 00:11:24,665
Hsiang-chun.

218
00:11:24,666 --> 00:11:26,291
Why is the vibe so tense in here?

219
00:11:28,583 --> 00:11:30,708
Have you prescribed KCL today?

220
00:11:31,875 --> 00:11:32,708
No, why?

221
00:11:34,708 --> 00:11:36,625
- Oh, it's nothing.
- Huh?

222
00:11:37,333 --> 00:11:38,375
[Wen-chih] Resus Room.

223
00:11:38,916 --> 00:11:39,875
Kuei-sheng has no pulse!

224
00:11:42,208 --> 00:11:44,540
[intense music playing]

225
00:11:44,541 --> 00:11:45,500
[Chao-i] Tung-yen.

226
00:11:46,375 --> 00:11:47,458
Tung-yen!

227
00:11:51,125 --> 00:11:52,332
[machine beeping]

228
00:11:52,333 --> 00:11:54,416
In three, two, one. Switch.

229
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,207
- No pulse.
- Epi, one milligram, IV push.

230
00:11:57,208 --> 00:11:58,290
- Yeah.
- [Geng-ming] Okay.

231
00:11:58,291 --> 00:11:59,625
[panting]

232
00:12:00,666 --> 00:12:02,208
Epi, one milligram, IV push.

233
00:12:02,875 --> 00:12:03,707
[Chao-i] Okay.

234
00:12:03,708 --> 00:12:04,750
[Su-ching] Done.

235
00:12:05,875 --> 00:12:07,166
[machine beeping rapidly]

236
00:12:08,166 --> 00:12:09,458
[Geng-ming] Still no pulse.

237
00:12:10,041 --> 00:12:11,457
Sine wave.

238
00:12:11,458 --> 00:12:12,541
I'll do it.

239
00:12:13,291 --> 00:12:15,583
- One calcium gluconate, four bicarb.
- [Su-ching] Got it.

240
00:12:16,916 --> 00:12:19,499
Dr. Huang, why do we see a sine wave?

241
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:22,666
Excessively high potassium,
most likely cause.

242
00:12:32,708 --> 00:12:34,332
[Wen-chih] One calcium gluconate, IV push.

243
00:12:34,333 --> 00:12:35,249
[Chao-i] Okay.

244
00:12:35,250 --> 00:12:36,583
[machine beeping]

245
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:41,625
- [Wen-chih] That's done.
- [Chao-i] Bicarb ready?

246
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:46,125
- [Wen-chih] Four bicarb, IV push.
- [Chao-i] Got it.

247
00:12:47,291 --> 00:12:48,625
- [Wen-chih] And done.
- [Chao-i] Okay.

248
00:12:55,583 --> 00:12:57,124
Dr. Huang, two minutes.

249
00:12:57,125 --> 00:12:58,833
[exhales]

250
00:13:01,916 --> 00:13:03,166
Got a pulse.

251
00:13:05,958 --> 00:13:08,790
How much longer does the ICU need?

252
00:13:08,791 --> 00:13:09,957
Send him up at once.

253
00:13:09,958 --> 00:13:11,124
- Okay.
- Shit.

254
00:13:11,125 --> 00:13:12,499
Hello, this is ER.

255
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,958
- We're transferring a patient.
- [Geng-ming] Dr. Huang!

256
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:16,875
Tung-yen.

257
00:13:17,666 --> 00:13:18,958
You didn't hear me before?

258
00:13:20,875 --> 00:13:21,707
What is this?

259
00:13:21,708 --> 00:13:23,416
Why didn't you come to help?

260
00:13:27,541 --> 00:13:28,957
I was typing up

261
00:13:28,958 --> 00:13:31,125
all this paperwork and I didn't hear you.

262
00:13:32,208 --> 00:13:33,583
Oh!

263
00:13:35,833 --> 00:13:36,832
You heard what I said.

264
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:39,415
You call yourself a genius R1?

265
00:13:39,416 --> 00:13:41,082
You're a spineless coward.

266
00:13:41,083 --> 00:13:43,875
- You're a disgrace.
- Hey! Hey.

267
00:13:45,791 --> 00:13:47,041
That's enough.

268
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:55,791
[pensive music playing]

269
00:14:13,916 --> 00:14:15,165
Mr. Wu, how are you?

270
00:14:15,166 --> 00:14:16,375
I'm Dr. Huang.

271
00:14:16,875 --> 00:14:19,582
So, uh, Dr. Tang
told me about your condition.

272
00:14:19,583 --> 00:14:22,332
I believe we can control it
with active treatment.

273
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:24,415
We have a new therapy
with almost no side effects,

274
00:14:24,416 --> 00:14:27,791
for which you can apply for insurance.
How does that sound?

275
00:14:28,541 --> 00:14:29,957
How much will it cost?

276
00:14:29,958 --> 00:14:33,165
You'd only be out of pocket
if insurance wasn't available.

277
00:14:33,166 --> 00:14:35,166
Roughly 100,000 a month.

278
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:38,124
[groans] But I don't have that much money.

279
00:14:38,125 --> 00:14:39,665
Well then, how about we do

280
00:14:39,666 --> 00:14:41,707
the synthetic
vascular graft surgery first?

281
00:14:41,708 --> 00:14:43,791
Then you start your chemo
as an outpatient.

282
00:14:44,916 --> 00:14:46,040
There's no way.

283
00:14:46,041 --> 00:14:48,833
If I get the vascular graft operation,

284
00:14:49,416 --> 00:14:51,083
I won't be able to set up the stall.

285
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,250
Which means
I won't be able to work anymore.

286
00:14:54,875 --> 00:14:56,999
[coughs]

287
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,208
You'll be okay.

288
00:14:58,916 --> 00:14:59,833
Just take it easy.

289
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:03,665
Once the oxygen's
made you feel a bit better,

290
00:15:03,666 --> 00:15:05,333
think again about the graft.

291
00:15:11,166 --> 00:15:12,583
I'm sorry, Dr. Huang.

292
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:14,708
They didn't take your advice.

293
00:15:15,708 --> 00:15:17,250
[groans] It's part of the job.

294
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,250
I visited your mom today.

295
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:22,665
Her condition was quite good.

296
00:15:22,666 --> 00:15:23,874
Uh, she asked me to remind you

297
00:15:23,875 --> 00:15:25,874
to drink lots of water
but don't hold your pee.

298
00:15:25,875 --> 00:15:26,874
- [sighs]
- [chuckles]

299
00:15:26,875 --> 00:15:28,999
Why'd she have to tell you all that?

300
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,499
Uh...

301
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:33,749
She also said you chose ER
so you could take care of her.

302
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:35,333
- Hmm?
- Hmm.

303
00:15:37,041 --> 00:15:38,500
You're a very devoted daughter.

304
00:15:40,166 --> 00:15:41,291
And an amazing doctor.

305
00:15:42,125 --> 00:15:44,124
You handled
the summary back there very well.

306
00:15:44,125 --> 00:15:46,207
It allowed me to get quickly up to speed.

307
00:15:46,208 --> 00:15:49,375
Dr. Huang,
can I join the new drug research team?

308
00:15:50,833 --> 00:15:52,082
Of course you can.

309
00:15:52,083 --> 00:15:54,415
Excellent juniors like you
are welcome anytime.

310
00:15:54,416 --> 00:15:55,666
[sighs in relief]

311
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,540
[Hsiu-ju] Take care when you're bathing

312
00:16:04,541 --> 00:16:07,165
and just make sure you keep
the wound dry if you can.

313
00:16:07,166 --> 00:16:10,415
Sometimes the medication we put on,
it will make it feel a little itchy.

314
00:16:10,416 --> 00:16:12,457
Do your best not to scratch though, okay?

315
00:16:12,458 --> 00:16:14,499
Now, can I book
the next appointment for you?

316
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,749
- Got a minute?
- Mmm.

317
00:16:15,750 --> 00:16:17,957
Have you seen the blood test
from that patient in resus?

318
00:16:17,958 --> 00:16:19,583
Why would I check someone else's report?

319
00:16:21,125 --> 00:16:22,166
Take a look.

320
00:16:23,958 --> 00:16:25,290
TENG KUEI-SHENG

321
00:16:25,291 --> 00:16:26,790
POTASSIUM

322
00:16:26,791 --> 00:16:28,707
[Hsi] Why is his potassium so high?

323
00:16:28,708 --> 00:16:31,082
When Teng Kuei-sheng was admitted,
his potassium was normal.

324
00:16:31,083 --> 00:16:32,666
Then it surged post-surgery.

325
00:16:33,250 --> 00:16:34,125
Something's off.

326
00:16:35,125 --> 00:16:39,041
And I just overheard the nurse say,
the KCL quantity doesn't match.

327
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:41,874
So, KCL's gone missing?

328
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,332
Yeah.

329
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:44,415
Excuse me.

330
00:16:44,416 --> 00:16:46,707
What were you two just talking about?

331
00:16:46,708 --> 00:16:49,000
My husband's resuscitation, was that it?

332
00:16:51,791 --> 00:16:55,500
[indistinct shouting]

333
00:17:00,833 --> 00:17:03,250
[shouting continues]

334
00:17:07,833 --> 00:17:08,958
[shouting stops]

335
00:17:11,125 --> 00:17:13,125
You were alone with my husband,
weren't you?

336
00:17:13,791 --> 00:17:15,791
Tell me. Do you wanna kill him?

337
00:17:16,875 --> 00:17:17,832
[Cheng-chun] Ma'am.

338
00:17:17,833 --> 00:17:21,665
I understand you're upset,
but there's no need to make accusations.

339
00:17:21,666 --> 00:17:23,082
[scoffs]

340
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:24,916
Teng Kuei-sheng is a loan shark.

341
00:17:25,833 --> 00:17:27,666
And how many deaths has he caused?

342
00:17:28,291 --> 00:17:29,582
Through violent tactics?

343
00:17:29,583 --> 00:17:31,833
It's a waste of our time and energy

344
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,000
- to try and save him.
- Hey.

345
00:17:35,375 --> 00:17:37,082
That's right. I hope that he dies.

346
00:17:37,083 --> 00:17:38,457
[indistinct shouting]

347
00:17:38,458 --> 00:17:40,707
[thug 1] Hey!
Who the hell do you think you are?

348
00:17:40,708 --> 00:17:43,291
[indistinct shouting]

349
00:17:45,708 --> 00:17:47,249
[thug 2] Come on!

350
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:48,166
[screams] Shut up!

351
00:17:54,541 --> 00:17:56,541
Dr. Chiang didn't inject him.

352
00:17:58,708 --> 00:17:59,791
It was him.

353
00:18:01,333 --> 00:18:04,375
I went to the triage station
to get myself a snack.

354
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:08,832
And I saw him go into the Resus Room
and rummage through the medical cart,

355
00:18:08,833 --> 00:18:10,332
and he took something out.

356
00:18:10,333 --> 00:18:11,958
Is that what you're playing?

357
00:18:13,083 --> 00:18:14,582
To get a doctor off the hook,

358
00:18:14,583 --> 00:18:16,040
you're smearing a patient's family?

359
00:18:16,041 --> 00:18:17,791
[Hsiang-chun] I saw you do it.

360
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:19,499
Why don't you search me?

361
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,750
Nothing here.

362
00:18:21,250 --> 00:18:22,082
Do it.

363
00:18:22,083 --> 00:18:24,374
[Hsiang-chun] Then he must have thrown it
all away somewhere.

364
00:18:24,375 --> 00:18:26,124
I really saw him going through the cart.

365
00:18:26,125 --> 00:18:28,000
If you lie again,
I'll cut out your tongue.

366
00:18:30,416 --> 00:18:32,791
Do you know what color KCL is, hmm?

367
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:34,416
It's yellow.

368
00:18:35,041 --> 00:18:38,125
- [thug 1] Oh, fuck. It's actually him.
- [thug 2] You think he's done something?

369
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:41,290
- Didn't see that coming.
- Surely not.

370
00:18:41,291 --> 00:18:43,249
- [thug 3] Yeah.
- [thug 4] What a damn coward.

371
00:18:43,250 --> 00:18:44,457
[thug 3] So what do we do now?

372
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:47,041
[thug 4] Hey, let's hear him out.
It better be good though.

373
00:18:48,916 --> 00:18:50,083
[chuckles] Fuck.

374
00:18:52,208 --> 00:18:54,291
Teng Kuei-sheng and I were ambushed today.

375
00:18:55,375 --> 00:18:58,375
Nansha Association thugs
rushed from two vehicles.

376
00:18:59,416 --> 00:19:00,916
Do you wanna know what he did?

377
00:19:02,750 --> 00:19:04,458
He pushed me out of the car and fled.

378
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:10,374
<i>How many years
have I been with Teng Kuei-sheng?</i>

379
00:19:10,375 --> 00:19:12,666
<i>How many times
have I risked my life for him?</i>

380
00:19:13,291 --> 00:19:15,083
<i>He pushed me out to die just like that.</i>

381
00:19:16,458 --> 00:19:18,874
After it happened,
there was only one thing on my mind.

382
00:19:18,875 --> 00:19:20,291
If I get back,

383
00:19:21,625 --> 00:19:22,707
I will kill him somehow.

384
00:19:22,708 --> 00:19:23,625
[grunts]

385
00:19:24,750 --> 00:19:25,583
[yells] Take him away.

386
00:19:33,083 --> 00:19:35,458
I will leave my husband in your hands.

387
00:19:37,666 --> 00:19:38,791
Let's go.

388
00:19:40,583 --> 00:19:42,999
Come on, move. You're a fucking ingrate.

389
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,208
Man, you are dead when we get back.

390
00:19:45,833 --> 00:19:46,875
[Cheng-chun] Are you okay?

391
00:19:49,416 --> 00:19:51,000
[indistinct chatter]

392
00:19:52,250 --> 00:19:53,750
[exhales]

393
00:20:03,958 --> 00:20:04,958
Thanks.

394
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,708
I'm the one who should thank you.

395
00:20:09,666 --> 00:20:11,749
I did see him go through the cart.

396
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:14,708
But I didn't actually see him
inject anything.

397
00:20:15,791 --> 00:20:17,666
Lucky the truth came out.

398
00:20:19,166 --> 00:20:20,375
Did it ever occur to you...

399
00:20:22,208 --> 00:20:24,457
that I might have been
the one who'd done it?

400
00:20:24,458 --> 00:20:27,082
[somber music playing]

401
00:20:27,083 --> 00:20:28,500
Do you trust me that much?

402
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:32,207
Of course.
You have professional medical skills.

403
00:20:32,208 --> 00:20:35,000
You're a really good doctor. And besides...

404
00:20:37,125 --> 00:20:38,875
And well,

405
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:40,750
I believe...

406
00:20:41,833 --> 00:20:44,125
the person I like wouldn't do that.

407
00:20:44,875 --> 00:20:45,832
Huh?

408
00:20:45,833 --> 00:20:47,666
Uh, I better get back to work.

409
00:21:28,083 --> 00:21:29,083
Oh, did I wake you?

410
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:33,125
How's your dad doing?

411
00:21:33,791 --> 00:21:34,958
He's okay.

412
00:21:36,125 --> 00:21:37,541
At least he's sleeping now.

413
00:21:40,041 --> 00:21:42,582
Oh. All these books are covered.

414
00:21:42,583 --> 00:21:44,208
My dad covered them.

415
00:21:44,916 --> 00:21:47,041
He told me to study hard for my future.

416
00:21:47,708 --> 00:21:49,165
So I won't be like him.

417
00:21:49,166 --> 00:21:51,291
I wanna get into college soon.

418
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,249
Graduate and then work.

419
00:21:53,250 --> 00:21:55,541
So I can earn money to take care of him.

420
00:21:58,041 --> 00:21:59,958
- Dr. Tang.
- Mmm?

421
00:22:00,791 --> 00:22:02,041
Thanks for checking on my dad.

422
00:22:03,708 --> 00:22:05,625
I really wanna study medicine,

423
00:22:06,625 --> 00:22:09,083
and become a doctor, like you.

424
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:19,583
[gentle music playing]

425
00:22:21,625 --> 00:22:24,541
- [groans softly]
- Oh, it's okay, Mom, it's me.

426
00:22:25,250 --> 00:22:26,541
[softly] I'm exhausted.

427
00:22:27,125 --> 00:22:28,625
I gotta lie down for a bit.

428
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:37,416
Ma.

429
00:22:38,583 --> 00:22:41,166
I met a patient like you today.

430
00:22:42,125 --> 00:22:43,415
He didn't want any help

431
00:22:43,416 --> 00:22:46,333
but I finally convinced him
to stay in the hospital.

432
00:22:48,458 --> 00:22:50,500
We need to cherish the time we have.

433
00:22:51,208 --> 00:22:53,415
Get the treatment when we need it.

434
00:22:53,416 --> 00:22:54,958
And live well, okay?

435
00:23:06,875 --> 00:23:07,875
[coughs]

436
00:23:15,458 --> 00:23:18,999
Today, lung cancer
has one of the highest mortality rates.

437
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,790
But now, we hope that can change.

438
00:23:20,791 --> 00:23:24,332
Our approach doesn't rely
on invasive traditional methods.

439
00:23:24,333 --> 00:23:26,874
Our approach
simply involves drawing blood.

440
00:23:26,875 --> 00:23:30,000
We call this new way
next-generation sequencing.

441
00:23:30,625 --> 00:23:33,374
We envision a future
where targeted genetic therapies

442
00:23:33,375 --> 00:23:37,166
will safeguard the health of all citizens
affected by cancer.

443
00:23:38,541 --> 00:23:39,374
And cut.

444
00:23:39,375 --> 00:23:40,790
- That okay?
- It was great.

445
00:23:40,791 --> 00:23:42,165
- You like it?
- Yeah. Well done.

446
00:23:42,166 --> 00:23:44,332
[director] Thank you, Dr. Huang.
That was a great take.

447
00:23:44,333 --> 00:23:46,499
We'll have a five-minute break.
We'll go again.

448
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:48,665
- Good job, Dr. Huang.
- Not at all. It's my duty.

449
00:23:48,666 --> 00:23:51,457
Hey, the pharmaceutical company
really liked what you did.

450
00:23:51,458 --> 00:23:53,665
Oh, well, that's great to hear.

451
00:23:53,666 --> 00:23:54,625
Um...

452
00:23:55,791 --> 00:23:57,457
Dr. Chuang,

453
00:23:57,458 --> 00:23:59,582
I was wondering if you knew

454
00:23:59,583 --> 00:24:00,625
who Director Cheng

455
00:24:01,416 --> 00:24:03,207
has in mind for the um...

456
00:24:03,208 --> 00:24:05,957
[clears throat] The Head of Department
of Internal Medicine.

457
00:24:05,958 --> 00:24:08,916
The position has been vacant a long time
and we need a leader.

458
00:24:09,791 --> 00:24:12,749
We still need to trouble you
for the new drugs paper though.

459
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:14,999
The pharmaceutical company will need that.

460
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:17,249
- Will that be okay?
- Yes, of course.

461
00:24:17,250 --> 00:24:19,083
- Great. Good work.
- Thank you.

462
00:24:23,041 --> 00:24:25,250
DR. HUANG YOU-CHANG

463
00:24:26,541 --> 00:24:28,499
You were given the time and the budget,

464
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:30,416
so why can't you find the problem?

465
00:24:31,916 --> 00:24:32,875
[loudly] Why not?

466
00:24:34,666 --> 00:24:36,290
Until this is solved,
no one is leaving here.

467
00:24:36,291 --> 00:24:37,458
Understand?

468
00:24:39,083 --> 00:24:39,957
Well, come on!

469
00:24:39,958 --> 00:24:41,832
Uh, Dr. Huang.

470
00:24:41,833 --> 00:24:44,040
I'd, uh, I'd like to leave the team.

471
00:24:44,041 --> 00:24:45,333
[female doctor] Same for me.

472
00:24:47,666 --> 00:24:48,540
Get out.

473
00:24:48,541 --> 00:24:49,582
Go home then.

474
00:24:49,583 --> 00:24:50,541
[yells] Get out!

475
00:25:02,125 --> 00:25:03,791
[phone vibrating]

476
00:25:04,833 --> 00:25:06,290
- [clears throat]
- [Li-te] <i>You-chang.</i>

477
00:25:06,291 --> 00:25:07,624
Yes, Dr. Chuang.

478
00:25:07,625 --> 00:25:09,915
<i>I'm having dinner
with the pharmaceutical reps now.</i>

479
00:25:09,916 --> 00:25:13,332
<i>Director Chang said he's optimistic
about Cheng-chun's paper.</i>

480
00:25:13,333 --> 00:25:14,999
<i>You need to step up.</i>

481
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:17,500
<i>Truth is Cheng-chun's
the one he wants to mentor.</i>

482
00:25:18,166 --> 00:25:21,915
<i>You know, if I hadn't kept supporting you
and putting in a good word,</i>

483
00:25:21,916 --> 00:25:23,749
<i>do you think you'd even have a shot</i>

484
00:25:23,750 --> 00:25:26,000
<i>at the Head of Department
of Internal Medicine?</i>

485
00:25:26,666 --> 00:25:28,082
<i>Don't disappoint me.</i>

486
00:25:28,083 --> 00:25:29,207
ALERT: TRIAL DATA BELOW TARGET

487
00:25:29,208 --> 00:25:31,166
[You-chang] No, sir.
Thank you, Dr. Chuang.

488
00:25:36,166 --> 00:25:38,791
[intense music playing]

489
00:25:54,041 --> 00:25:56,124
[groans]

490
00:25:56,125 --> 00:25:57,665
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

491
00:25:57,666 --> 00:25:58,958
Save me.

492
00:25:59,708 --> 00:26:00,540
Okay.

493
00:26:00,541 --> 00:26:01,665
[groans]

494
00:26:01,666 --> 00:26:02,624
My stomach hurts.

495
00:26:02,625 --> 00:26:04,999
- All right, let's find you a bed.
- Okay.

496
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,165
- [groans]
- Okay.

497
00:26:06,166 --> 00:26:07,083
There you go.

498
00:26:07,666 --> 00:26:09,915
- What kind of pain do you have, sir?
- Uh. Stomach ache.

499
00:26:09,916 --> 00:26:12,165
- Can you hear me?
- [Hsiu-ju] He's putting it on, you know.

500
00:26:12,166 --> 00:26:14,708
Oh, Nurse Hsiu-ju, what do you mean?

501
00:26:16,083 --> 00:26:17,290
That there is Lai Pi-tan.

502
00:26:17,291 --> 00:26:19,290
Shows up here every now and again.

503
00:26:19,291 --> 00:26:20,957
He owes a lot of medical fees.

504
00:26:20,958 --> 00:26:22,332
He's on our blacklist.

505
00:26:22,333 --> 00:26:23,957
Targets rookies like you.

506
00:26:23,958 --> 00:26:25,207
A nice, friendly R1.

507
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:27,499
And finds a random reason
to take a bed here.

508
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:29,415
You should just ignore him, okay?

509
00:26:29,416 --> 00:26:31,082
He'll leave once he's had a sleep anyway.

510
00:26:31,083 --> 00:26:33,332
No, but he said he had a stomachache
and he's just fainted.

511
00:26:33,333 --> 00:26:35,040
You're sure we don't need to examine him?

512
00:26:35,041 --> 00:26:36,790
- [Pi-tan groans]
- Up to you.

513
00:26:36,791 --> 00:26:38,291
- [groans]
- [Geng-ming] Okay.

514
00:26:38,958 --> 00:26:40,457
[woman screams]

515
00:26:40,458 --> 00:26:41,707
Oh no! Sir!

516
00:26:41,708 --> 00:26:44,124
No, you can't do that here.
No-- I'm so sorry, miss.

517
00:26:44,125 --> 00:26:45,207
- Sir, please.
- [Pi-tan] Hey.

518
00:26:45,208 --> 00:26:47,415
Hsiang-chun,
get the cleaning team down here.

519
00:26:47,416 --> 00:26:48,791
Come on. Come with me.

520
00:26:51,291 --> 00:26:53,165
The family reported her unconscious,

521
00:26:53,166 --> 00:26:55,707
but by the time
they noticed it had been three hours.

522
00:26:55,708 --> 00:26:57,832
Let's have her connected to a monitor.

523
00:26:57,833 --> 00:26:59,207
Then draw blood.

524
00:26:59,208 --> 00:27:00,750
- And arrange for a CT.
- Sure.

525
00:27:01,916 --> 00:27:02,750
Doctor?

526
00:27:04,208 --> 00:27:07,124
My mom had a stroke three years ago.
How is she now?

527
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:08,582
Um. Here's the thing.

528
00:27:08,583 --> 00:27:11,249
Your mom's age is a factor here.

529
00:27:11,250 --> 00:27:14,249
Also she has some chronic health issues.

530
00:27:14,250 --> 00:27:18,249
If a need for resuscitation
does present itself,

531
00:27:18,250 --> 00:27:22,291
it is important for you as a family
to decide the best way to proceed.

532
00:27:26,333 --> 00:27:28,791
- [groans]
- [PA system chimes]

533
00:27:29,375 --> 00:27:31,458
[nurse over PA system]
<i>Triage nurse required in B3.</i>

534
00:27:32,375 --> 00:27:34,625
Oh, uh... Dr. Cheng, what's the matter?

535
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:37,749
We've had several complaints.

536
00:27:37,750 --> 00:27:40,374
He's already seriously affected
other patients.

537
00:27:40,375 --> 00:27:42,500
I understand he's caused some problems.

538
00:27:43,833 --> 00:27:45,915
Unhoused people still need medical care.

539
00:27:45,916 --> 00:27:47,249
[scoffs]

540
00:27:47,250 --> 00:27:48,833
Unhoused? The man's a bum.

541
00:27:49,750 --> 00:27:51,165
You young people are so hung up

542
00:27:51,166 --> 00:27:53,207
on your politically correct terms,
aren't you?

543
00:27:53,208 --> 00:27:54,666
Is there a difference?

544
00:27:57,833 --> 00:27:59,874
Due to self-reported chest tightness,

545
00:27:59,875 --> 00:28:02,249
this man has had over a dozen ECGs.

546
00:28:02,250 --> 00:28:05,249
Presents with high levels of alcohol
in his blood every time.

547
00:28:05,250 --> 00:28:06,915
And he's never paid any of his fees.

548
00:28:06,916 --> 00:28:09,582
- It really hurts this time, I swear.
- Of course it hurts.

549
00:28:09,583 --> 00:28:10,875
You drink too much alcohol.

550
00:28:13,250 --> 00:28:14,750
[groans]

551
00:28:15,791 --> 00:28:18,000
I want this bed clear within the hour.

552
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:23,624
[Geng-ming] Hsiu-ju. Please.

553
00:28:23,625 --> 00:28:25,457
Can you set up an IV drip?

554
00:28:25,458 --> 00:28:28,082
I'll prescribe Ketorolac
to help with his pain.

555
00:28:28,083 --> 00:28:29,957
I wanna make sure he's okay. Please.

556
00:28:29,958 --> 00:28:32,999
[sighs] I really don't know
what to do with you.

557
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:33,916
Okay.

558
00:28:34,666 --> 00:28:35,708
Thank you so much.

559
00:28:40,958 --> 00:28:42,083
[groans]

560
00:28:51,041 --> 00:28:52,208
How's mom doing?

561
00:28:55,291 --> 00:28:56,208
Tell me!

562
00:28:57,625 --> 00:28:58,915
- Hi, doctor.
- Hi.

563
00:28:58,916 --> 00:29:00,333
May I ask how Mom's doing now?

564
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:05,290
Uh, we see from the CT results
there is some serious cerebral bleeding.

565
00:29:05,291 --> 00:29:08,291
We will need to intubate
to assist with her breathing now.

566
00:29:09,458 --> 00:29:13,541
Have you discussed with your family
what you'd like to happen with your mom?

567
00:29:14,375 --> 00:29:17,124
Well... I mean, she's very old now.

568
00:29:17,125 --> 00:29:20,790
I hope that she can pass peacefully
and doesn't have to suffer anymore.

569
00:29:20,791 --> 00:29:21,916
This is our mother.

570
00:29:22,666 --> 00:29:23,750
Why would you even say that?

571
00:29:24,375 --> 00:29:27,040
Look, she's in pain
and she doesn't know what's going on.

572
00:29:27,041 --> 00:29:29,665
If mom were conscious,
she'd never agree to live this way.

573
00:29:29,666 --> 00:29:31,124
How would you know what she wants?

574
00:29:31,125 --> 00:29:32,957
You've had
nothing to do with her for years.

575
00:29:32,958 --> 00:29:35,415
And I'm the one
who's been doing everything for her.

576
00:29:35,416 --> 00:29:38,000
There is no way you can make that call!

577
00:29:38,833 --> 00:29:39,708
Sorry.

578
00:29:40,833 --> 00:29:43,374
I feel terrible that all the care
has been left to you.

579
00:29:43,375 --> 00:29:44,707
But these are two separate matters.

580
00:29:44,708 --> 00:29:46,708
And resuscitating her

581
00:29:47,541 --> 00:29:48,707
will increase her suffering.

582
00:29:48,708 --> 00:29:51,249
- Is that what you really want for her?
- I'll suffer more if she goes!

583
00:29:51,250 --> 00:29:52,541
I'm sorry.

584
00:29:55,291 --> 00:29:56,375
[Hsi] Dr. He?

585
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:57,833
Uh...

586
00:29:59,166 --> 00:30:01,707
I know this is a difficult situation.

587
00:30:01,708 --> 00:30:05,000
Please let us know what you'd like to do
once you've discussed it.

588
00:30:27,125 --> 00:30:28,250
[sighs]

589
00:30:31,416 --> 00:30:32,333
[sighs wearily]

590
00:30:33,375 --> 00:30:34,708
Dr. He?

591
00:30:37,541 --> 00:30:39,000
I know my mom will die.

592
00:30:39,958 --> 00:30:41,791
It's coming sooner or later.

593
00:30:43,458 --> 00:30:45,125
But I find it so hard

594
00:30:46,041 --> 00:30:47,375
to let go of her.

595
00:30:48,708 --> 00:30:50,875
[melancholy music playing]

596
00:30:54,333 --> 00:30:55,666
If you were me,

597
00:30:58,583 --> 00:30:59,583
what would you do?

598
00:31:04,791 --> 00:31:05,625
Uh...

599
00:31:06,125 --> 00:31:09,708
To be honest with you,
my mom and I don't... get along.

600
00:31:11,583 --> 00:31:12,665
[chuckles softly]

601
00:31:12,666 --> 00:31:16,125
So I don't really know
what I would say to her in your situation.

602
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:19,833
I can only give you
my considered medical advice.

603
00:31:20,541 --> 00:31:22,416
Looking at her condition now,

604
00:31:23,375 --> 00:31:25,458
if we do begin life support for her,

605
00:31:27,083 --> 00:31:27,958
we can't go back.

606
00:31:29,208 --> 00:31:31,707
She'll become dependent
on the life support machines

607
00:31:31,708 --> 00:31:32,791
for her survival.

608
00:31:35,833 --> 00:31:36,833
Should I stop?

609
00:31:41,666 --> 00:31:43,375
Can I... stop?

610
00:31:51,333 --> 00:31:52,208
[groans]

611
00:31:53,416 --> 00:31:54,791
[Chao-i] He's escaped again, huh?

612
00:31:55,666 --> 00:31:58,040
You ever think about
all the medical resources

613
00:31:58,041 --> 00:32:01,499
used on a guy like this
when other people really need them?

614
00:32:01,500 --> 00:32:03,790
The ER is a very practical place.

615
00:32:03,791 --> 00:32:05,541
People come and then they go.

616
00:32:06,458 --> 00:32:08,249
When your shift's done,
just clock off and leave.

617
00:32:08,250 --> 00:32:09,540
Don't take it home with you.

618
00:32:09,541 --> 00:32:11,458
You get me, rookie?

619
00:32:12,708 --> 00:32:13,625
Mmm.

620
00:32:32,916 --> 00:32:34,040
[soft music playing]

621
00:32:34,041 --> 00:32:36,000
[man] Okay. Now let's put this on.

622
00:32:36,750 --> 00:32:39,082
So, can I just check,
do you have all your stuff here?

623
00:32:39,083 --> 00:32:40,582
[Geng-ming's dad] Hello, everyone.

624
00:32:40,583 --> 00:32:43,290
Glad you could all be here.
My name is Mr. Lin.

625
00:32:43,291 --> 00:32:45,415
I'm the organizer of today's joint event

626
00:32:45,416 --> 00:32:47,874
for sighted
and visually impaired participants.

627
00:32:47,875 --> 00:32:50,999
Big welcome to everyone
who's new here today.

628
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:52,457
We only really have one rule,

629
00:32:52,458 --> 00:32:54,874
and that's to have as much fun as you can.

630
00:32:54,875 --> 00:32:56,290
Come on, make some noise.

631
00:32:56,291 --> 00:32:58,374
Let me know if we're gonna have fun today.

632
00:32:58,375 --> 00:33:00,833
- [crowd cheering]
- There we go.

633
00:33:02,291 --> 00:33:03,665
Come on, come on.

634
00:33:03,666 --> 00:33:06,583
- It's safe. It's fun, I promise.
- [crowd gasping]

635
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:10,999
[people cheering]

636
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:12,915
[women laughing]

637
00:33:12,916 --> 00:33:14,999
Okay, jump. One, two.

638
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,832
- [laughs]
- Wow, you did it.

639
00:33:16,833 --> 00:33:18,249
[both laughing]

640
00:33:18,250 --> 00:33:20,374
- Hey, do you guys want some water?
- Oh, I got one. Thanks.

641
00:33:20,375 --> 00:33:22,374
- How about you guys? Here.
- Yeah, one bottle. Thanks.

642
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:24,500
[both laughing]

643
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:27,999
Water?

644
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,458
- Thank you.
- No worries.

645
00:33:30,291 --> 00:33:31,124
[sighs]

646
00:33:31,125 --> 00:33:32,665
Haven't seen you guys here before.

647
00:33:32,666 --> 00:33:34,999
- Mmm.
- Your mom's having fun, huh?

648
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,083
[giggles]

649
00:33:37,041 --> 00:33:40,041
I think Mom
still has some pretty good balance.

650
00:33:41,041 --> 00:33:43,083
It was six years ago, she lost her sight.

651
00:33:43,833 --> 00:33:45,875
Oh. What happened?

652
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:48,249
Acute glaucoma.

653
00:33:48,250 --> 00:33:52,791
Due to the doctor's misdiagnosis,
she missed optimal time for treatment.

654
00:33:53,708 --> 00:33:56,625
My mom couldn't accept it
for a very long time.

655
00:33:57,583 --> 00:33:58,916
I was really worried.

656
00:33:59,875 --> 00:34:01,291
But she's better now.

657
00:34:02,083 --> 00:34:03,791
She's a lot more willing to come out.

658
00:34:05,666 --> 00:34:06,749
My dad was born blind.

659
00:34:06,750 --> 00:34:09,957
But I think he's wilder
than sighted people sometimes.

660
00:34:09,958 --> 00:34:12,040
[laughs] Don't worry.

661
00:34:12,041 --> 00:34:13,499
- No, he's fine!
- [both laughing]

662
00:34:13,500 --> 00:34:15,791
- I'm fine. Oh good.
- Don't jump so high next time.

663
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:17,916
- Oh! Ah.
- [woman] Let me help you.

664
00:34:19,041 --> 00:34:21,665
Here you are.
Everyone here calls me Siaoming.

665
00:34:21,666 --> 00:34:23,790
You know, family members need support too.

666
00:34:23,791 --> 00:34:26,375
If you ever find you need some help,
well, just call.

667
00:34:28,916 --> 00:34:30,540
Hmm. Thank you.

668
00:34:30,541 --> 00:34:32,000
Mmm. Great.

669
00:34:34,541 --> 00:34:37,457
LOVE FOR THE BLIND STUDIO
323 QINGPU RD.

670
00:34:37,458 --> 00:34:40,125
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

671
00:34:42,416 --> 00:34:43,540
- Hey.
- Huh?

672
00:34:43,541 --> 00:34:45,625
- What are you doing back here?
- [chuckles]

673
00:34:46,583 --> 00:34:49,415
I forgot the notes Dr. Chou gave me.
I just gotta look something up.

674
00:34:49,416 --> 00:34:51,416
Oh. Dr. Chou.

675
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:52,832
Good for you.

676
00:34:52,833 --> 00:34:53,958
[chuckles]

677
00:34:54,708 --> 00:34:55,916
Oh, hey, wait.

678
00:34:56,541 --> 00:34:57,625
[softly] Come here, come here.

679
00:34:58,708 --> 00:35:01,582
Do you know the guy sleeping? Over there?

680
00:35:01,583 --> 00:35:03,665
He's been waiting here for a long time.

681
00:35:03,666 --> 00:35:06,333
Kept asking for you
but he wouldn't say why.

682
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:11,833
- Mr. Lai.
- [exclaims]

683
00:35:13,083 --> 00:35:15,583
Huh? Oh, don't scare me, dude.

684
00:35:17,583 --> 00:35:18,500
Why'd you run away?

685
00:35:20,333 --> 00:35:22,999
Well, I heard
you were gonna inject me with, uh,

686
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:24,624
that horrible painkiller.

687
00:35:24,625 --> 00:35:26,499
Keto or something.

688
00:35:26,500 --> 00:35:30,290
Last time I had that, I almost died.
Bad reaction.

689
00:35:30,291 --> 00:35:31,707
Never again, man.

690
00:35:31,708 --> 00:35:33,457
Hey, did you happen to see a...

691
00:35:33,458 --> 00:35:35,291
Uh, forget it.

692
00:35:36,625 --> 00:35:39,166
- Mmm.
- I thought you would have thrown it out.

693
00:35:41,166 --> 00:35:42,708
Well, there's no money anyway.

694
00:35:43,291 --> 00:35:45,249
- I should just throw it.
- No way.

695
00:35:45,250 --> 00:35:47,000
Don't you have
a photo of your wife in there?

696
00:35:47,625 --> 00:35:49,291
- [chuckles] Oh, yeah.
- Yeah.

697
00:35:51,291 --> 00:35:52,166
Look.

698
00:35:52,708 --> 00:35:54,207
Beauty, right?

699
00:35:54,208 --> 00:35:55,125
Mmm.

700
00:35:55,916 --> 00:35:57,457
She walked out on me.

701
00:35:57,458 --> 00:35:58,957
It's the way it goes.

702
00:35:58,958 --> 00:36:00,791
I drank too much, you know.

703
00:36:03,208 --> 00:36:06,165
I've been doing odd jobs
where I can, you know.

704
00:36:06,166 --> 00:36:07,415
I wanna fly straight.

705
00:36:07,416 --> 00:36:08,582
Stay outta trouble.

706
00:36:08,583 --> 00:36:11,541
Hopefully if that works,
you know, she might come back.

707
00:36:14,583 --> 00:36:16,500
[inhales deeply]

708
00:36:17,958 --> 00:36:19,333
Hey, don't scratch, okay?

709
00:36:20,250 --> 00:36:21,500
It might be cellulitis.

710
00:36:23,083 --> 00:36:24,541
Here. Take this.

711
00:36:25,416 --> 00:36:26,583
Put it on each day.

712
00:36:27,333 --> 00:36:29,790
There's also some gauze
and some cotton swabs here.

713
00:36:29,791 --> 00:36:30,874
Change them daily.

714
00:36:30,875 --> 00:36:32,540
Here. Take it.

715
00:36:32,541 --> 00:36:33,958
Well, gotta go.

716
00:36:34,958 --> 00:36:36,665
Oh, hey, man, uh...

717
00:36:36,666 --> 00:36:38,915
Just call me Pi-tan, okay?

718
00:36:38,916 --> 00:36:40,290
It's what the nurses call me.

719
00:36:40,291 --> 00:36:41,625
It sounds friendlier, right?

720
00:36:42,791 --> 00:36:43,708
I'm Dr. Lin.

721
00:36:45,500 --> 00:36:46,500
Hey, doc.

722
00:36:49,083 --> 00:36:49,958
Thanks, man.

723
00:36:57,083 --> 00:36:59,040
Is your headache feeling better?

724
00:36:59,041 --> 00:37:00,915
Uh, yeah, a little.

725
00:37:00,916 --> 00:37:02,332
- Okay.
- Dr. He?

726
00:37:02,333 --> 00:37:05,291
Wang Li in Bed 7
is in a critical condition.

727
00:37:09,333 --> 00:37:11,125
[crying]

728
00:37:12,041 --> 00:37:12,874
Hey, ma'am.

729
00:37:12,875 --> 00:37:14,250
Can you hear me?

730
00:37:15,583 --> 00:37:16,541
Ms. Liu.

731
00:37:17,750 --> 00:37:20,166
Get your family to come
as quick as they can.

732
00:37:22,166 --> 00:37:24,125
[melancholy music playing]

733
00:37:30,125 --> 00:37:32,083
[sobbing softly]

734
00:37:37,958 --> 00:37:40,541
[machine beeping rapidly]

735
00:37:46,208 --> 00:37:48,208
Dr. He. Save my mom.

736
00:37:52,375 --> 00:37:53,291
Are you sure?

737
00:37:55,833 --> 00:37:56,666
Please.

738
00:37:59,208 --> 00:38:00,208
CPR.

739
00:38:03,416 --> 00:38:04,999
Family members, please step outside.

740
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:06,958
Sorry guys, just give us a moment.

741
00:38:08,458 --> 00:38:09,291
Let's go.

742
00:38:12,791 --> 00:38:13,915
What are they doing?

743
00:38:13,916 --> 00:38:16,290
Didn't we agree not to resuscitate her?

744
00:38:16,291 --> 00:38:18,124
She suffered all her life.

745
00:38:18,125 --> 00:38:20,083
You can't let her go, even now?

746
00:38:20,750 --> 00:38:23,125
We can't give her this dignity
after the life she's had?

747
00:38:23,750 --> 00:38:25,791
How can you be so selfish?

748
00:38:26,375 --> 00:38:27,249
Prep for intubation.

749
00:38:27,250 --> 00:38:29,000
You're hurting her right now.
Do you know that?

750
00:38:29,791 --> 00:38:33,125
[yells] All I know is that Mom deserves
more than having a daughter like you!

751
00:38:44,625 --> 00:38:46,000
- [sighs]
- [Yu-hua] You okay?

752
00:38:53,791 --> 00:38:54,916
Dr. He.

753
00:38:55,583 --> 00:38:56,458
Do you think...

754
00:38:58,083 --> 00:39:00,125
resuscitating my mom...

755
00:39:01,708 --> 00:39:03,250
was the wrong decision?

756
00:39:09,583 --> 00:39:11,207
Do you remember you asked me earlier?

757
00:39:11,208 --> 00:39:13,875
What I would do if I were you?

758
00:39:15,083 --> 00:39:16,458
If I wasn't a doctor,

759
00:39:17,791 --> 00:39:20,750
or if I hadn't seen patients
continue to suffer,

760
00:39:21,708 --> 00:39:23,000
I would have wanted to save her.

761
00:39:24,125 --> 00:39:27,541
I wanna be with her
as long as I possibly can.

762
00:39:30,125 --> 00:39:32,291
Do you understand why that is?

763
00:39:36,625 --> 00:39:38,083
Because when she dies,

764
00:39:40,583 --> 00:39:42,124
my brother gets the house.

765
00:39:42,125 --> 00:39:44,457
[pensive music playing]

766
00:39:44,458 --> 00:39:46,291
I'll have nowhere to live.

767
00:39:47,083 --> 00:39:49,166
Mom left all her assets to my brother.

768
00:39:50,791 --> 00:39:53,000
But I'm the only one
who takes care of her.

769
00:39:55,583 --> 00:39:57,791
She didn't think about me at all.

770
00:39:59,375 --> 00:40:00,875
After all of these years.

771
00:40:03,041 --> 00:40:05,500
No matter how nice I am to her,

772
00:40:06,166 --> 00:40:08,625
it seems my brother
is the only one she cares about.

773
00:40:10,750 --> 00:40:12,166
Does that sound fair?

774
00:40:14,041 --> 00:40:16,666
So that's why I want her to live on.

775
00:40:17,333 --> 00:40:19,125
Even if the quality is poor.

776
00:40:19,958 --> 00:40:20,958
I know...

777
00:40:25,791 --> 00:40:27,916
I won't survive without her.

778
00:40:33,625 --> 00:40:35,541
Really, she owes it to me.

779
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:41,125
Thank you for saving my mom.

780
00:40:51,708 --> 00:40:52,833
[sighs]

781
00:41:04,541 --> 00:41:06,375
[phone vibrating]

782
00:41:16,416 --> 00:41:17,500
[blows air]

783
00:41:20,333 --> 00:41:21,833
Didn't you say you'll quit smoking?

784
00:41:23,750 --> 00:41:25,040
Hey, you know what?

785
00:41:25,041 --> 00:41:27,791
I resuscitated a really old lady today.

786
00:41:28,791 --> 00:41:30,540
Thought I was saving her. [chuckles]

787
00:41:30,541 --> 00:41:32,458
Turns out though,

788
00:41:34,791 --> 00:41:35,875
I harmed her.

789
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:38,665
You know what, though?

790
00:41:38,666 --> 00:41:39,916
I feel like a sort of...

791
00:41:40,708 --> 00:41:43,208
Almost like an accomplice, in some way.

792
00:41:45,250 --> 00:41:47,749
I'm helping her daughter
take revenge on her.

793
00:41:47,750 --> 00:41:49,208
[Yu-hua sighs]

794
00:41:53,083 --> 00:41:54,541
You know what blows my mind though?

795
00:41:55,208 --> 00:41:56,874
There's a bunch of gangsters here.

796
00:41:56,875 --> 00:41:59,124
But this morning, I'm the one in trouble.

797
00:41:59,125 --> 00:42:01,665
Over an hour,
I was interrogated in that hearing.

798
00:42:01,666 --> 00:42:03,957
You know it's a good thing
that you weren't there.

799
00:42:03,958 --> 00:42:05,040
You would've lost your shit.

800
00:42:05,041 --> 00:42:06,958
It was such a waste of time.

801
00:42:08,916 --> 00:42:11,707
And do you know
what the most crazy part is?

802
00:42:11,708 --> 00:42:15,750
There's no legal way
to stop gangsters gathering in a hospital.

803
00:42:16,500 --> 00:42:18,207
What exactly is going on in this world?

804
00:42:18,208 --> 00:42:20,874
We can't distinguish
between right and wrong.

805
00:42:20,875 --> 00:42:22,708
[somber music playing]

806
00:42:23,958 --> 00:42:25,916
- Yu-hua. Come here.
- [Yu-hua shuddering]

807
00:42:30,166 --> 00:42:31,583
What happened, exactly?

808
00:42:39,875 --> 00:42:41,625
I got a phone call from the lawyer.

809
00:42:42,416 --> 00:42:44,750
As a result of the medical dispute case,

810
00:42:45,625 --> 00:42:46,750
I'm being sued.

811
00:43:00,625 --> 00:43:02,333
I don't know what I did wrong.

812
00:43:14,833 --> 00:43:16,833
[closing theme music playing]
